== Description ==

Increases mana profits with amount of spells cast. Focuses on gaining more shards and increasing profits through his spells and upgrades.

Unique [[Sources|Source]]: Arcanaspring, replaces Spell Fountain.

== Basic Design ==
Arcanist primarily profits by casting a lot of spells. He has a greatly increased ability to earn spell shards, thanks to spells like {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Spellstaff Of Chamaon}}, which allows the autoclicks from the 4 apprentice summons to earn a lot more spell shards, and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Lightning Bolt}}, which is a much more powerful combination of {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Spell Focus}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Magic Missile}}. At very high levels he can leverage these spell shards to cast {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Arcane Infusion}}, an incredibly expensive spell that increases his character ability power with every cast.

He also has 2 new spells that scale based on the number of casts: {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Karnaphen's Spellshroud}}, and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Radiant Pools}}. Both of these are powerful new incantations that greatly increase profits, especially combined with his character ability, which also scales off total spells cast.

At a high level, he also gains access to {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Jas'Aham's Missile Storm}}, a persistent spell that grants an ever-increasing number of casts to other spells on the bar, allowing him to stack his spells cast, and the abilities of {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Karnaphen's Spellshroud}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Radiant Pools}}, and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Arcane Infusion}} incredibly quickly. Stacking this persistent also helps in the future with [[Archon]].

